{"id": "9f73b752-c8d2-4955-84cb-a80e9c76b120", "slug": "nexusflow-messaging", "title": "NexusFlow - Messaging", "description": "Nexusflow Messaging Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"NexusFlow - Messaging\"\ndescription: \"Nexusflow Messaging Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#34D399\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#34D399\"\n  background: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  surface: \"#4B5563\"\n  text-primary: \"#111827\"\n  text-secondary: \"#4B5563\"\n  border: \"#E5E7EB\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# NexusFlow - Messaging\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Sourany Phomhome (@sou). Views: 4; favorites: 3; remixes: 1.\nTags: hero, section, css, headline, marketing, interactive.\n## Overview\nNexusflow Messaging Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.\n\nRefine your messaging. We handle the delivery. Utilize NexusFlow to broadcast crisp, impactful notifications to your audience — reliably and securely across all channels. Begin Free Trial N 353° N N S W E\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Refine your messaging. We handle the delivery..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #34D399, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #34D399, background #FFFFFF, surface #4B5563, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>NexusFlow - Messaging</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@200;300;400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\n            background-color: #030a07; /* Very dark green/black */\n            color: #ffffff;\n            overflow-x: hidden;\n        }\n\n        /* Subtle static dot grid for texture behind webgl */\n        .bg-pattern {\n            background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px);\n            background-size: 32px 32px;\n        }\n\n        /* Faint glow effects */\n        .glow-line-h {\n            background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.2), transparent);\n        }\n        .glow-line-v {\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.2), transparent);\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-pattern min-h-screen relative flex items-center justify-center selection:bg-emerald-500/30\">\n\n    <!-- WebGL Background Canvas Container -->\n    <div id=\"webgl-bg\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none opacity-80\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Decorative Corner Markers -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none overflow-hidden max-w-[1600px] mx-auto\">\n        <div class=\"absolute top-12 left-12 w-2 h-2 border border-emerald-500/30 opacity-50\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-12 right-12 w-2 h-2 border border-emerald-500/30 opacity-50\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-12 left-12 w-2 h-2 border border-emerald-500/30 opacity-50\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-12 right-12 w-2 h-2 border border-emerald-500/30 opacity-50\"></div>\n\n        <!-- Faint structural lines -->\n        <div class=\"absolute top-12 left-0 w-full h-[1px] glow-line-h opacity-30\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 left-12 w-[1px] h-full glow-line-v opacity-30\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 right-12 w-[1px] h-full glow-line-v opacity-30\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"relative z-10 w-full max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-8 items-center\">\n\n        <!-- Left Column: Copy -->\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col max-w-xl\">\n            <!-- Icon -->\n            <div class=\"w-12 h-12 rounded-xl border border-white/5 bg-white/5 flex items-center justify-center mb-10 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(52,211,153,0.1)]\">\n                <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:leaf-linear\" class=\"text-emerald-400 text-2xl\"></iconify-icon>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Heading -->\n            <!-- Using lighter weights and tight tracking for large text per requirements -->\n            <h1 class=\"text-5xl sm:text-6xl lg:text-[5.5rem] leading-[1.05] font-light tracking-tighter mb-8 text-white/95\">\n                Refine your<br>messaging.<br>We handle the<br>delivery.\n            </h1>\n\n            <!-- Subtext -->\n            <p class=\"text-gray-400 text-lg sm:text-xl font-light leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-md\">\n                Utilize NexusFlow to broadcast crisp, impactful notifications to your audience — reliably and securely across all channels.\n            </p>\n\n            <!-- CTA Button -->\n            <div>\n                <button class=\"bg-white text-black font-medium text-sm px-7 py-3.5 rounded flex items-center gap-2 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors duration-200 group\">\n                    Begin Free Trial\n                    <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:arrow-right-up-linear\" class=\"text-lg text-black/60 group-hover:text-black transition-colors\"></iconify-icon>\n                </button>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Right Column: Animated Compass -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-center items-center relative w-full h-full min-h-[400px]\">\n            <!-- Compass Container -->\n            <div id=\"compass-wrapper\" class=\"relative w-full max-w-[450px] aspect-square\">\n                <!-- Three.js Canvas injected here -->\n\n                <!-- HTML UI Overlay for perfect typography -->\n                <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-10 pointer-events-none flex flex-col items-center justify-center\">\n\n                    <!-- Center Data -->\n                    <div class=\"flex flex-col items-center translate-y-[-2px]\">\n                        <span class=\"text-emerald-400 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.3em] mb-2 opacity-90 drop-shadow-[0_0_8px_rgba(52,211,153,0.8)]\">N</span>\n                        <!-- The degree number that updates via JS -->\n                        <span id=\"compass-degree\" class=\"text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-light tracking-tight text-white/95\">353°</span>\n                        <span class=\"text-gray-500 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.3em] mt-2 opacity-60\">N</span>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <!-- Outer Labels (N, E, S, W) -->\n                    <div class=\"absolute top-[18%] left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 text-emerald-400/80 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest drop-shadow-[0_0_5px_rgba(52,211,153,0.5)]\">N</div>\n                    <div class=\"absolute bottom-[18%] left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 text-gray-500/60 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest\">S</div>\n                    <div class=\"absolute left-[18%] top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-gray-500/60 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest\">W</div>\n                    <div class=\"absolute right-[18%] top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-gray-500/60 text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest\">E</div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- WebGL & Animation Logic -->\n    <script>\n        // Ensure script runs after DOM is ready\n        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n\n            // --- 1. BACKGROUND SCENE ---\n            const bgContainer = document.getElementById('webgl-bg');\n            const bgScene = new THREE.Scene();\n            bgScene.fog = new THREE.FogExp2(0x030a07, 0.0015);\n\n            const bgCamera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 1000);\n            bgCamera.position.z = 100;\n\n            const bgRenderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ alpha: true, antialias: true });\n            bgRenderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n            bgRenderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n            bgContainer.appendChild(bgRenderer.domElement);\n\n            // Particles\n            const particlesGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n            const particlesCount = 400;\n            const posArray = new Float32Array(particlesCount * 3);\n            for(let i = 0; i < particlesCount * 3; i+=3) {\n                posArray[i] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 500; // x\n                posArray[i+1] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 300; // y\n                posArray[i+2] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 200; // z\n            }\n            particlesGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(posArray, 3));\n            const particlesMat = new THREE.PointsMaterial({\n                size: 1.2,\n                color: 0x34d399, // Emerald 400\n                transparent: true,\n                opacity: 0.3,\n                blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending\n            });\n            const particlesMesh = new THREE.Points(particlesGeo, particlesMat);\n            bgScene.add(particlesMesh);\n\n            // Glowing Streaks (Horizontal lines)\n            const streaksGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n            const streakPts = [];\n            for(let i=0; i<25; i++) {\n                let y = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 200;\n                let z = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 100;\n                let x = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 400;\n                let len = Math.random() * 80 + 20;\n                streakPts.push(x, y, z);\n                streakPts.push(x + len, y, z);\n            }\n            streaksGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(streakPts, 3));\n            const streaksMat = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({\n                color: 0x34d399,\n                transparent: true,\n                opacity: 0.15,\n                blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending\n            });\n            const streaksMesh = new THREE.LineSegments(streaksGeo, streaksMat);\n            bgScene.add(streaksMesh);\n\n\n            // --- 2. COMPASS SCENE ---\n            const compWrapper = document.getElementById('compass-wrapper');\n            let compW = compWrapper.clientWidth;\n            let compH = compWrapper.clientHeight;\n\n            const compScene = new THREE.Scene();\n            const compCamera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(40, compW / compH, 0.1, 1000);\n            compCamera.position.z = 32;\n\n            const compRenderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ alpha: true, antialias: true });\n            compRenderer.setSize(compW, compH);\n            compRenderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n            compRenderer.domElement.style.position = 'absolute';\n            compRenderer.domElement.style.inset = '0';\n            compRenderer.domElement.style.zIndex = '1';\n            compWrapper.appendChild(compRenderer.domElement);\n\n            // Lighting to make it look metallic/glassy\n            const ambientLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.5);\n            compScene.add(ambientLight);\n\n            const dirLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1);\n            dirLight.position.set(10, 20, 15);\n            compScene.add(dirLight);\n\n            const greenLight = new THREE.PointLight(0x34d399, 2, 50);\n            greenLight.position.set(0, 10, 5);\n            compScene.add(greenLight);\n\n            // Compass Object Group\n            const compassGroup = new THREE.Group();\n            // Tilt the compass slightly for a 3D effect\n            compassGroup.rotation.x = -0.15;\n            compScene.add(compassGroup);\n\n            // Materials\n            const darkMetalMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x050a08, roughness: 0.2, metalness: 0.8 });\n            const midMetalMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x111a15, roughness: 0.4, metalness: 0.6 });\n            const tickMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x333333 });\n            const majorTickMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x555555 });\n            const glowMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x34d399 }); // Emerald 400\n\n            // 1. Outer Bezel Ring\n            const bezelGeo = new THREE.TorusGeometry(10.5, 0.4, 32, 128);\n            const bezelMesh = new THREE.Mesh(bezelGeo, darkMetalMat);\n            compassGroup.add(bezelMesh);\n\n            // 2. Base Plate (Dark Background)\n            const baseGeo = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(10.4, 10.4, 0.2, 64);\n            const baseMesh = new THREE.Mesh(baseGeo, darkMetalMat);\n            baseMesh.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\n            baseMesh.position.z = -0.2;\n            compassGroup.add(baseMesh);\n\n            // 3. Static Tick Marks Group (Outer Ring)\n            const staticTicksGroup = new THREE.Group();\n            for (let i = 0; i < 360; i += 2) {\n                const isMajor = i % 10 === 0;\n                const isCardinal = i % 90 === 0;\n\n                let h = 0.2;\n                let mat = tickMat;\n                if(isCardinal) { h = 0.6; mat = majorTickMat; }\n                else if(isMajor) { h = 0.4; mat = majorTickMat; }\n\n                // Top (North) marker is glowing green\n                if (i === 0) { mat = glowMat; h = 0.8; }\n\n                const tGeo = new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.04, h, 0.05);\n                const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(tGeo, mat);\n\n                const radius = 9.8;\n                const angle = (i * Math.PI) / 180;\n                mesh.position.x = Math.sin(angle) * radius;\n                mesh.position.y = Math.cos(angle) * radius;\n                mesh.rotation.z = -angle;\n                mesh.position.z = 0.1;\n\n                staticTicksGroup.add(mesh);\n            }\n            compassGroup.add(staticTicksGroup);\n\n            // Function to generate a canvas texture for numbers\n            function createNumberTexture() {\n                const size = 1024;\n                const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\n                canvas.width = size;\n                canvas.height = size;\n                const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n                const center = size / 2;\n                const radius = size * 0.40; // Position of numbers\n\n                ctx.clearRect(0, 0, size, size);\n                ctx.fillStyle = '#4b5563'; // Tailwind gray-600 roughly\n                ctx.font = '300 24px Inter, sans-serif';\n                ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n                ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';\n\n                for (let i = 0; i < 360; i += 30) {\n                    // Skip 0, 90, 180, 270 where letters are\n                    if (i % 90 === 0) continue;\n\n                    const angle = (i - 90) * (Math.PI / 180);\n                    const x = center + Math.cos(angle) * radius;\n                    const y = center + Math.sin(angle) * radius;\n\n                    ctx.save();\n                    ctx.translate(x, y);\n                    ctx.rotate(angle + Math.PI / 2); // orient text towards center\n                    ctx.fillText(i.toString(), 0, 0);\n                    ctx.restore();\n                }\n\n                const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\n                texture.anisotropy = compRenderer.capabilities.getMaxAnisotropy();\n                return texture;\n            }\n\n            // 4. Inner Rotating Dial Group\n            const innerDialGroup = new THREE.Group();\n            compassGroup.add(innerDialGroup);\n\n            // Inner Plate\n            const innerBaseGeo = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(7.5, 7.5, 0.2, 64);\n            const innerBaseMesh = new THREE.Mesh(innerBaseGeo, midMetalMat);\n            innerBaseMesh.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\n            innerBaseMesh.position.z = 0.1;\n            innerDialGroup.add(innerBaseMesh);\n\n            // Sub-ticks on inner dial\n            for (let i = 0; i < 360; i += 5) {\n                const isMajor = i % 10 === 0;\n                const tGeo = new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.03, isMajor ? 0.3 : 0.15, 0.05);\n                const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(tGeo, isMajor ? majorTickMat : tickMat);\n                const radius = 7.2;\n                const angle = (i * Math.PI) / 180;\n                mesh.position.x = Math.sin(angle) * radius;\n                mesh.position.y = Math.cos(angle) * radius;\n                mesh.rotation.z = -angle;\n                mesh.position.z = 0.25;\n                innerDialGroup.add(mesh);\n            }\n\n            // Number Ring (Mapped Texture)\n            const numRingGeo = new THREE.RingGeometry(5, 7.4, 64);\n            const numRingMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({\n                map: createNumberTexture(),\n                transparent: true,\n                opacity: 0.8,\n                side: THREE.DoubleSide\n            });\n            const numRingMesh = new THREE.Mesh(numRingGeo, numRingMat);\n            numRingMesh.position.z = 0.26;\n            innerDialGroup.add(numRingMesh);\n\n            // Green Indicator Line pointing North on the inner dial\n            const indicatorGeo = new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.08, 1.2, 0.1);\n            const indicatorMesh = new THREE.Mesh(indicatorGeo, glowMat);\n            indicatorMesh.position.y = 6.4; // Positioned near top edge of inner dial\n            indicatorMesh.position.z = 0.3;\n            innerDialGroup.add(indicatorMesh);\n\n            // Center Ring Detail\n            const centerRingGeo = new THREE.TorusGeometry(4.8, 0.03, 16, 64);\n            const centerRingMesh = new THREE.Mesh(centerRingGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({color: 0x333333}));\n            centerRingMesh.position.z = 0.26;\n            innerDialGroup.add(centerRingMesh);\n\n\n            // --- ANIMATION LOOP ---\n            const clock = new THREE.Clock();\n            const degreeEl = document.getElementById('compass-degree');\n\n            // Logic variables\n            let baseDegree = 353; // Base degree matching design\n            let currentRotation = 0;\n\n            function animate() {\n                requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n                const elapsedTime = clock.getElapsedTime();\n\n                // 1. Animate Background\n                // Move particles\n                const pPositions = particlesMesh.geometry.attributes.position.array;\n                for(let i=0; i<particlesCount * 3; i+=3) {\n                    pPositions[i] -= 0.6; // Drift left\n                    if(pPositions[i] < -250) pPositions[i] = 250; // Wrap\n                    // Gentle vertical wave\n                    pPositions[i+1] += Math.sin(elapsedTime * 1.5 + i) * 0.03;\n                }\n                particlesMesh.geometry.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;\n\n                // Move streaks\n                const sPositions = streaksMesh.geometry.attributes.position.array;\n                for(let i=0; i<sPositions.length; i+=6) {\n                    // Move start and end points\n                    const speed = 1.5 + Math.random() * 0.5;\n                    sPositions[i] -= speed;\n                    sPositions[i+3] -= speed;\n\n                    if(sPositions[i] < -250) {\n                        const len = sPositions[i+3] - sPositions[i];\n                        sPositions[i] = 250;\n                        sPositions[i+3] = 250 + len;\n                    }\n                }\n                streaksMesh.geometry.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;\n\n\n                // 2. Animate Compass\n                // Create a smooth, organic back-and-forth movement around the base degree\n                // Using multiple sine waves for unpredictable natural feel\n                const offset = Math.sin(elapsedTime * 0.4) * 8 + Math.cos(elapsedTime * 0.7) * 4;\n                const targetDegree = baseDegree + offset;\n\n                // Calculate radians for rotation\n                // Compass rotates opposite to the numbers visually\n                const targetRad = (targetDegree * Math.PI) / 180;\n\n                // Smooth interpolation (lerp)\n                currentRotation += (targetRad - currentRotation) * 0.05;\n\n                // Apply rotation to inner dial\n                innerDialGroup.rotation.z = currentRotation;\n\n                // Update HTML Text (Clamp to 0-359 integer)\n                let displayDeg = Math.floor((currentRotation * 180 / Math.PI)) % 360;\n                if(displayDeg < 0) displayDeg += 360;\n\n                // Pad with zeros if desired, but reference shows \"353°\"\n                degreeEl.innerText = `${displayDeg}°`;\n\n                // Add very subtle floating to the whole compass group\n                compassGroup.position.y = Math.sin(elapsedTime * 1) * 0.2;\n                compassGroup.rotation.y = Math.sin(elapsedTime * 0.5) * 0.05;\n\n                // Render both scenes\n                bgRenderer.render(bgScene, bgCamera);\n                compRenderer.render(compScene, compCamera);\n            }\n\n            animate();\n\n            // --- RESIZE HANDLER ---\n            window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n                // Update Background\n                bgCamera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;\n                bgCamera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n                bgRenderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n\n                // Update Compass\n                compW = compWrapper.clientWidth;\n                compH = compWrapper.clientHeight;\n                compCamera.aspect = compW / compH;\n                compCamera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n                compRenderer.setSize(compW, compH);\n            });\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "nexusflow-messaging.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/nexusflow-messaging.jpg", "source_name": "nexusflow-messaging-DESIGN.md", "views": 78, "forks": 5, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "8bd0314a-9525-4a13-996e-2c37cbd9e514", "created_at": "2026-05-01T16:18:09.070118+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T23:42:38.214625+00:00"}